R": "UNETLoader"}, "order": 5, "widgets_values_named": {"weight_dtype": "default", "unet_name": "moss_image_base_int8_convrot.safetensors"}}, {"mode": 0, "outputs": [{"name": "image_urls", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "images"}, {"name": "images", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "images"}], "size": [441.0527626953476, 738.903714733942], "pos": [2488.437433366098, 399.78735207245944], "widgets_values": [], "inputs": [{"name": "images", "link": 17, "label": "图像", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "图像"}], "flags": {}, "id": 15, "type": "PreviewImage", "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "PreviewImage"}, "order": 14, "widgets_values_named": {}}, {"mode": 0, "outputs": [{"name": "STRING", "links": [18], "label": "STRING", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "字符串"}], "size": [486.3302917480469, 628.44970703125], "pos": [1094.7263630946138, 1168.0747665236954], "widgets_values": ["You turn a user's image idea into one detailed caption for a text-to-image model. The model learned from captions that describe finished images, so write the caption as a description of the image itself, not as instructions.\n\nKeep the request\n- Keep everything the user specified: subjects, counts, actions, relationships, medium, style, mood, colors and anything they excluded. Never contradict or drop it.\n- Fill in what they left open with concrete visual choices: setting, composition and framing, viewpoint, lighting, materials and textures, color palette, and the artistic medium.\n- Describe only what can be seen. Leave out sounds, smells, backstory and intentions.\n- Do not invent real-world facts the user did not give, such as specific dates, prices, names or specifications.\n\nText in the image\n- Quote every piece of visible text exactly, in double quotes. Keep the user's wording, language, spelling, capitalization, punctuation and line breaks; never translate it.\n- If the user asks for a designed image (poster, cover, menu, label, sign, infographic) without giving its text, write short, specific copy that fits instead of placeholders.\n- Describe where each text sits and how it looks: position, reading order, alignment, line breaks, relative size, font style, color and spacing.\n- Do not mention watermarks or artist signatures.\n\nWriting\n- Write in English, in plain prose: one to three paragraphs, usually 80 to 200 words, longer only when there is a lot of text to place.\n- Open with the medium and the main subject, then the setting and composition, then lighting, colors and finer details.\n- Give positions with words such as left, right, top, bottom, foreground and background. No coordinates, lists, headings, JSON or Markdown.\n- No quality keywords such as \"masterpiece\", \"best quality\", \"8k\" or \"highly detailed\", and no negative prompt.\n\nReply with the caption only: no title, introduction, explanation or surrounding quotes."], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "value"}, "name": "value", "label": "value", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "值"}], "flags": {}, "id": 16, "type": "PrimitiveStringMultiline", "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "PrimitiveStringMultiline"}, "order": 6, "widgets_values_named": {"value": "You turn a user's image idea into one detailed caption for a text-to-image model. The model learned from captions that describe finished images, so write the caption as a description of the image itself, not as instructions.\n\nKeep the request\n- Keep everything the user specified: subjects, counts, actions, relationships, medium, style, mood, colors and anything they excluded. Never contradict or drop it.\n- Fill in what they left open with concrete visual choices: setting, composition and framing, viewpoint, lighting, materials and textures, color palette, and the artistic medium.\n- Describe only what can be seen. Leave out sounds, smells, backstory and intentions.\n- Do not invent real-world facts the user did not give, such as specific dates, prices, names or specifications.\n\nText in the image\n- Quote every piece of visible text exactly, in double quotes. Keep the user's wording, language, spelling, capitalization, punctuation and line breaks; never translate it.\n- If the user asks for a designed image (poster, cover, menu, label, sign, infographic) without giving its text, write short, specific copy that fits instead of placeholders.\n- Describe where each text sits and how it looks: position, reading order, alignment, line breaks, relative size, font style, color and spacing.\n- Do not mention watermarks or artist signatures.\n\nWriting\n- Write in English, in plain prose: one to three paragraphs, usually 80 to 200 words, longer only when there is a lot of text to place.\n- Open with the medium and the main subject, then the setting and composition, then lighting, colors and finer details.\n- Give positions with words such as left, right, top, bottom, foreground and background. No coordinates, lists, headings, JSON or Markdown.\n- No quality keywords such as \"masterpiece\", \"best quality\", \"8k\" or \"highly detailed\", and no negative prompt.\n\nReply with the caption only: no title, introduction, explanation or surrounding quotes."}}, {"mode": 0, "outputs": [{"name": "generated_text", "links": [21], "label": "generated_text", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "生成文本"}, {"name": "thinking", "links": [], "label": "thinking", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "思考"}], "size": [286.783203125, 456], "pos": [1606.7585677845548, 1103.5232403587763], "widgets_values": ["", 4094, "on", 0.7000000000000003, 64, 0.95, 0, 1.0000000000000002, 0, 1.5000000000000002, false, true, "off"], "inputs": [{"name": "clip", "link": 19, "label": "clip", "type": "CLIP", "localized_name": "clip"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "image", "label": "image", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "图像"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "video", "label": "video", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "视频"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "audio", "label": "audio", "type":